  "hints": [
    "Sort intervals by start time first using sorted(intervals, key=lambda iv: (iv[0], iv[1])).",
    "Walk sorted intervals: if merged is empty or merged[-1][1] < cur[0], append [cur[0], cur[1]]; otherwise extend merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], cur[1]).",
    "Pseudocode:\n  if not intervals: return []\n  ordered = sorted(intervals)\n  merged = [list(ordered[0])]\n  for start, end in ordered[1:]:\n      if start <= merged[-1][1]: merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], end)\n      else: merged.append([start, end])\n  return merged"
  ],
